{"name":"Trumpeter","hex":"#907baa","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"trumpeter","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Someone who plays a trumpet.","Any of three species of bird in the genus Psophia from South America named for the trumpeting threat call of the males."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/trumpeter"}],"entries":[{"title":"Trumpet","blocks":[{"text":"The trumpet is a brass instrument. The most common type of trumpet is a transposing instrument in B♭, with pitches sounding a whole step lower than written. The trumpet family includes instruments ranging from the piccolo trumpet, with the highest register in the brass family, to the bass trumpet, pitched one octave below the standard B♭ or C trumpet."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/12/Yamaha_Trumpet_YTR-8335LA_crop.jpg/330px-Yamaha_Trumpet_YTR-8335LA_crop.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Trumpet"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/29/Musicians_at_the_coal_yard_-_DPLA_-_654d5920548ca26c571a5337d7807c60.jpg/500px-Musicians_at_the_coal_yard_-_DPLA_-_654d5920548ca26c571a5337d7807c60.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/29/Musicians_at_the_coal_yard_-_DPLA_-_654d5920548ca26c571a5337d7807c60.jpg/500px-Musicians_at_the_coal_yard_-_DPLA_-_654d5920548ca26c571a5337d7807c60.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Trio of trumpeters in Toledo, Ohio, approximately 1940","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMusicians_at_the_coal_yard_-_DPLA_-_654d5920548ca26c571a5337d7807c60.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bf/Trompette_d%27argent_et_sa_sourdine_en_bois_du_tombeau_de_Tout%C3%A2nkhamon_2.jpg/500px-Trompette_d%27argent_et_sa_sourdine_en_bo